## Findings

### Must-fix — the narrowed export contradicts the committed export contract

The governing c1 spec requires:

> “the flat plain-git LEDGER of the emitted `PY_S11CC1_*` objects”  
> — [S11c_c1_SHARED_PHYSICS.md §7, lines 560–564](/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger_v3/directives/S11c_c1_SHARED_PHYSICS.md:560)

D1 likewise says:

> “Export every object S9’s `MAIN` package emits… Mechanical, ⛔ no per-object judgement, and it errs toward exporting more.”  
> — [S9_REWRITE_PLAN.md, lines 210–213](/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger_v3/S9_REWRITE_PLAN.md:210)

The directive instead says:

> “Export … a **strict subset**”  
> — [build directive, lines 96–99](/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger_v3/directives/S11c_c1_sympy_build_directive.md:96)

and explicitly excludes primary §3 objects such as the Hermitian/reactive split, regime/parity views, Fredholm condition, loci, and dissipation/energy package:

> “⛔ **NOT exported — emit-to-stdout ONLY**…”  
> — [build directive, lines 113–123](/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger_v3/directives/S11c_c1_sympy_build_directive.md:113)

Those are not merely §5 control packages. They are declared primary §3a/§3b outputs in [§4 lines 358–365](/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger_v3/directives/S11c_c1_SHARED_PHYSICS.md:358). The directive therefore cannot legitimately “refine D1” from primary-emitted objects to next-consumer-only objects. F1–F9 contain no authority for that selection change; F6 governs publication completeness, while F9 governs collision keys.

The narrowing rationale also introduces unsupported future physics:

> “c2 re-derives its own dissipation and loci on the coupled self-energy operator”  
> — [build directive, lines 113–115](/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger_v3/directives/S11c_c1_sympy_build_directive.md:113)

The authority assigns c2 only the fold, closed-kernel re-extraction, and resulting self-energy [§0 lines 34–38](/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger_v3/directives/S11c_c1_SHARED_PHYSICS.md:34); it does not assign c2 a dissipation/locus re-derivation. Moreover, profile-conditioned singular loci are reserved for S11c-d [§3b lines 297–304](/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger_v3/directives/S11c_c1_SHARED_PHYSICS.md:297).

This is a wrong-export finding even though the immediate c2 dependency set itself is complete. The size constraint requires an authority/spec change or a different representation; the build directive cannot silently amend §7/D1.

